  "body": "Reported by a user in chat.\n\n## What happens\n\nA ribbon button that is on (toggled), for example **Paths** or **Deviate** in the Inspect group, shows only part of its highlight. This occurs when the button is activated, and also when the pointer hovers over a toggled button. The defect is in the ribbon. It is most visible with the themes. The user saw it in the light theme.\n\nThe user's sample image (light theme, Inspect group) shows **Paths** and **Deviate** toggled on, each with a pale red fill behind the icon and the label. **Frame** and **Simulate** are off and have no fill.\n\n<img width=\"273\" height=\"88\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a1d15318-8258-4a1f-97ad-370ad90192b8\" />\n\n## Expected\n\nA toggled button has one complete highlight, with or without hover. The highlight is the same in each theme.\n\n## Where to look\n\n`crates/ui/src/egui_app/painted.rs`, `cell()` (lines 54-112 on main):\n\n- The fill order is: pressed `accent`, then toggled `selection_bg`, then hovered `field_hover`. A toggled cell that is hovered paints only `selection_bg`. The hover has no visible effect on the fill.\n- The icon ink is `contrast::on_fill(bg)`. The label ink is always `pal.text` (or `text_faint`). The two inks do not follow the same rule. On a theme's `selection_bg`, the icon and the label can look different. This can be the cause for the activated state without hover.\n- `ribbon_tabs` in `crates/ui/src/egui_app/panes.rs` (near line 1107) uses its own hover and active rule.\n\nThe root cause is not confirmed. Reproduce it in the light theme and in one more theme first.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A toggled ribbon button has one complete, consistent highlight in each shipped theme, with and without hover.\n- The icon ink and the label ink on a filled cell follow one rule.\n- A structural test in `crates/ui` pins the state that `cell()` paints for toggled, hovered, and toggled plus hovered. The test asserts the state, not a colour or a size.\n",
